Subject: starting a playlist on KDE works even before the first display

A defect fix, not a feature. The same circle as with «Apply» (patch 0010):
on KDE the daemon gets a display only once the waywallen Plasma plugin is
assigned as the desktop wallpaper, and Rexon assigns it when a playlist
starts. The vendor playlist list chooses targets one by one: without a
display the start button is grey until the person picks «All» by hand
(VM Arch + Plasma 6.8.2, 30.10.2026).

Since v0.6.0 the neutral part of the edit is upstream (waywallen#370:
starting on «All» without displays and «an empty display set does not
play»). Only our part remains:

* `hasPlayTarget`: with zero targets starting is available even without
  choosing «All», if `W.App.playWithoutDisplays` (the decision is the core's,
  `waywallen_kde_plugin::play_without_displays`, the same `apply_gate` as the
  transport's). The Rexon transport holds the `playlist_activate` frame until
  plasmashell registers a display.
* `togglePlayback`: without displays the target is «all desktops», like the
  vendor «all» (`selectAll()`: empty targets + attaching new displays). With
  real displays upstream behaviour does not change.
---
diff --git a/ui/qml/page/wallpaper/PlaylistListSheetState.qml b/ui/qml/page/wallpaper/PlaylistListSheetState.qml
index 56ceb37..f564344 100644
--- a/ui/qml/page/wallpaper/PlaylistListSheetState.qml
+++ b/ui/qml/page/wallpaper/PlaylistListSheetState.qml
@@ -32,7 +32,15 @@ QtObject {
     readonly property bool mutationQuerying: playlistMutation.querying || playlistCreateMutation.querying
     readonly property bool createQuerying: playlistCreateMutation.querying
     readonly property var playlists: playlistListQuery.playlists || []
-    readonly property bool hasPlayTarget: targetState.allTargets || targetState.hasSelection
+    // REXON EDIT (a defect fix, not a feature): on KDE a display
+    // appears only once the wallpaper plugin is assigned, and Rexon
+    // assigns it when a playlist starts — without this branch, starting on a fresh
+    // system was unavailable until the person picked «All» by hand. While there are
+    // no displays, the target is «all desktops»; the Rexon transport holds the frame
+    // until a display registers. The edit lives in
+    // patches/0011-playlist-without-displays-on-kde.patch.
+    readonly property bool playWithoutDisplays: !targetState.hasTargets && W.App.playWithoutDisplays
+    readonly property bool hasPlayTarget: targetState.allTargets || targetState.hasSelection || playWithoutDisplays
 
     Component.onCompleted: {
         if (!playlistSheetSettings.targetScopeMigrated) {
@@ -92,6 +100,11 @@ QtObject {
             playlistPlaybackMutation.deactivate(targetState.wireTargets, targetState.allTargets ? playlist.id : 0);
             return;
         }
+        if (root.playWithoutDisplays && !targetState.allTargets) {
+            // REXON EDIT: «all desktops» — like the vendor «all»
+            // (empty targets and attaching new displays).
+            targetState.selectAll();
+        }
         playlistPlaybackMutation.activate(playlist.id, targetState.wireTargets, targetState.allTargets);
     }
 
